## Errors & Mistakes
- Three Bash calls used `echo ====` as a separator; zsh treats a leading `=`
  as an equals expansion and aborted with "=== not found". Quote separators.
- A grep call passed paths through an unquoted `$S` variable; zsh does not
  word-split, so ugrep saw one nonexistent path. Reran with literal paths.
- Large reads (the audit guide, the SKILL.md batch) got persisted to files
  instead of returned; re-read them with the Read tool.

